  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;The proposed development,\r\nby reason of the means of entrance for two of the three proposed flats, sited along\r\nthe narrow side passageway, would result in unsafe and indirect means of\r\nentrance. By reason of the internal configuration of proposed Flat 2, the\r\ndining room would not be afforded aspect or natural light representing a poor\r\nstandard of internal accommodation. The proposals are considered to fail to\r\nimplement Secure by Design or inclusive design principles, represent poor\r\ndesign and negatively impact future occupiers living conditions regarding internal\r\nquality of accommodation and sense of privacy by virtue of the routing of\r\noccupiers/visitors in proximity past the ground floor window serving a bedroom\r\nof proposed Flat 2.&amp;nbsp; In this way, the\r\nproposals are considered to conflict with Paragraph 135 of the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (NPPF, 2024) and Policies D5, D6 and D11 London Plan\r\n(2021), as well as Policy GR1.A and GR1.B(g) of the Harrow Local Plan\r\n(2021-2041) which seeks to ensure proposals achieve a high standard of design\r\nand layout and ensure Secure by Design principles are adopted into development\r\nproposals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
  "decision": "Refused",
  "appeal_decision": null,
